What changed
Scripted step: there is a new recovery_mode="scripted_step" in actions.py. When the wire is touched, the leg's thigh and calf targets are replaced by a foot trajectory, converted to joint angles with 2-link inverse kinematics in the leg's sagittal plane. The trajectory has four stages:
back off 12 cm;
lift 20 cm;
advance 30 cm over the wire;
lower the foot to standing height. The ab/ad joint stays on the walking policy, and the leg blends back over 6 steps afterwards. The same code serves all four legs.
Plumbing: the new parameters are step_* fields on ResidualRecoveryActionCfg. They are passed through env_cfg_residual.py and exposed as flags on d5_58_per_leg_recovery_window.py. The existing hybrid mode and the contact-gated option from last round are unchanged.
Logging: the hybrid-only actuator columns in the CSV now read 0.0 in scripted-step mode, instead of crashing.
