Why FL stumbled
The FL step failed because of the walking gait, not the step geometry. I added all four foot heights to the CSV and compared FL and FR at entry:

FL: the wire contact lands at the same moment the trot starts swinging FR and RL. Lifting FL immediately puts three feet in the air, and the body drops from 0.31 m to about 0.19 m. The leg can't fold shorter than about 0.13 m, so the foot only reaches 6–8 cm, below the 10.6 cm wire.
FR: the other feet stay planted during the lift, which is why FR worked.
The fix
What it does: a new step_wait_for_swing option holds the leg on the walking policy until its own foot lifts above 4 cm. That is FL's swing onset, when the diagonal pair is planted. There's a 14-step fallback if the foot never lifts. The step then runs as before.
Where it lives: the option is in actions.py and is off by default. In d5_58_per_leg_recovery_window.py it auto-enables for FL only.
Why FL only: the flag hurt the other legs. FR dropped from 3/4 to 0/4 crossing, and RR from 4/4 to 3/4. RL stayed at 3/4.
