What caused the seed-3 failures
Both failures have the same cause as the FL stumble:

FR seed 3: FL and RR also leave the ground mid-step, so only RL is planted and the body drops to 0.15 m.
RL seed 3: RL is a supporting leg when the retract starts. The foot never leaves the ground and the body sinks to 0.20 m.
A step takes about 26 control steps, which is longer than a trot half-period. The other legs keep cycling, so one leg's step can leave too few feet on the ground.

What I added
A new opt-in step_freeze_others option holds the other nine joints at the standing pose while the step runs, then blends them back to the walking policy.

I tested the option on all four legs, with 4 seeds each:

RL: it fixes RL, from 3/4 to 4/4.
FL, FR, RR: it breaks all three, each going to 0/4. The body still sags to about 0.23 m, and the calf stays 7–9 cm behind the wire. These legs need the body's forward motion to carry the calf over.
So the script now picks defaults per leg:

Leg	Setting (default in the script)	Crossing	Min body height
FL	wait for own swing onset	4/4	0.26–0.28 m
FR	immediate step	3/4 (seed 3 fails)	0.21–0.22 m (0.15 on the failure)
RL	other legs frozen	4/4	0.25 m
RR	immediate step	4/4	0.27–0.30 m
That is 15 of 16 runs crossing the wire, with FR seed 3 the only failure.

